main/dinit-dbus: make the dbus-daemon service provider explicit for cross.

The -dinit autopackage's service files say "depends-on: dbus-daemon", so
the 001_runtime_deps pkg hook must find an installed package providing
svc:/usvc:dbus-daemon in the (sys)root at package time. On a NATIVE
build that provider (dbus-dinit, an install_if autopackage of main/dbus)
arrives by accident: checkdepends = ["dbus"] installs dbus, and
dbus + dinit-chimera trip dbus-dinit's install_if. Cross builds skip
checkdepends entirely (cbuild core/dependencies.py gates them on
`not pkg.profile().cross`), nothing pulls dbus into the cross sysroot,
the install_if never fires, and the hook dies with

  ERROR:   usvc: dbus-daemon (unknown provider)
  hint: add package providing 'dbus-daemon' to 'makedepends'

Do what the hint says: add dbus-dinit to makedepends so the provider is
present regardless of build mode. Found cross-building main/iwd (which
depends on dinit-dbus) for the self-built armv7 repo; native builds are
unaffected (the dep was already installed transitively).

diff --git a/main/dinit-dbus/template.py b/main/dinit-dbus/template.py
--- a/main/dinit-dbus/template.py
+++ b/main/dinit-dbus/template.py
@@ -4,7 +4,10 @@ pkgrel = 0
 _gitrev = "5662aa890b08e7daec58942fdaae5b105cb881af"
 build_style = "meson"
 hostmakedepends = ["meson", "pkgconf"]
-makedepends = ["dinit-chimera", "dbus-devel", "libdinitctl-devel"]
+# dbus-dinit: provides svc:/usvc:dbus-daemon for the runtime-deps service
+# scan; native builds get it implicitly (checkdepends dbus + install_if),
+# cross builds skip checkdepends so it must be explicit
+makedepends = ["dbus-devel", "dbus-dinit", "dinit-chimera", "libdinitctl-devel"]
 checkdepends = ["dbus"]
 depends = ["dbus"]
 replaces = ["dbus-dinit<1.14.10-r14"]
